{
  "title": "55: al-Rahmaan الرحمن",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاَلرَّحْمٰنُۙ‏(1)\nAR-RAHMAAN.\nThe All-beneficent\nعَلَّمَ الْقُرْاٰنَؕ‏(2)\nA’LLAMAL QURAAN.\nhas taught the Quran.\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَۙ‏(3)\nKHALAQAL INSAAN.\nHe created man,\nعَلَّمَهُ الْبَيَانَ‏(4)\nA’LLAMAHUL BAYAAN.\n[and] taught him articulate speech.\nاَلشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ بِحُسْبَانٍ‏(5)\nASH-SHAMSO WAL-QAMARO BE HUSBAANIN.\nThe sun and the moon are [disposed] calculatedly,\nوَّالنَّجْمُ وَالشَّجَرُ يَسْجُدٰنِ‏(6)\nWAN-NAJMO WASH-SHAJARO YASJODAAN.\nand the herb and the tree prostrate [to Allah].\nوَالسَّمَآءَ رَفَعَهَا وَوَضَعَ الْمِيْزَانَۙ‏(7)\nWAS-SAMAAA-A RAFA-A’HAA WA-WAZA-A’L MEEZAAN.\nHe raised the heaven high and set up the balance,\nاَلَّا تَطْغَوْا فِى الْمِيْزَانِ‏(8)\nALLAA TATGHAW FIL MEEZAAN.\ndeclaring, ‘Do not infringe the balance!\nوَاَقِيْمُوا الْوَزْنَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا تُخْسِرُوا الْمِيْزَانَ‏(9)\nWA AQEEMUL WAZNA BIL QISTE WA LAA TUKHSERUL MEEZAAN.\nMaintain the weights with justice, and do not shorten the balance!’\nوَالْاَرْضَ وَضَعَهَا لِلْاَنَامِۙ‏(10)\nWAL ARZA WA ZA-A’HAA LIL ANAAM.\nAnd the earth—He laid it out for mankind.\nفِيْهَا فَاكِهَةٌ  ۙ وَّالنَّخْلُ ذَاتُ الْاَكْمَامِ ۖ‏(11)\nFEEHAA FAAKEHATUNW WAN-NAKHLO ZAATUL AKMAAM.\nIn it are fruits and date-palms with sheaths,\nوَالْحَبُّ ذُو الْعَصْفِ وَالرَّيْحَانُۚ‏(12)\nWAL-HABBO ZUL-A’SFE WAR-RAYHAAN.\ngrain with husk, and fragrant herbs.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(13)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nخَلَقَ الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ صَلْصَالٍ كَالْفَخَّارِۙ‏(14)\nKHALAQAL INSAANA MIN SALSAALIN KAL-FAKHKHAAR.\nHe created man out of dry clay, like the potter’s,\nوَخَلَقَ الْجَآنَّ مِنْ مَّارِجٍ مِّنْ نَّارٍۚ‏(15)\nWA KHALAQAL JAAAN-NA MIN MAAREJIM MIN NAAR.\nand created the jinn out of a flame of a fire.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(16)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nرَبُّ الْمَشْرِقَيْنِ وَ رَبُّ الْمَغْرِبَيْنِۚ‏(17)\nRABBUL MASHREQAYNE WA RABBUL MAGHREBAYN.\nLord of the two easts, and Lord of the two wests!\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(18)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nمَرَجَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ يَلْتَقِيٰنِۙ‏(19)\nMARAJAL BAHRAYNE YALTAQEYAAN.\nHe merged the two seas, meeting each other.\nبَيْنَهُمَا بَرْزَخٌ لَّا يَبْغِيٰنِۚ‏(20)\nBAYNAHOMAA BARZAKHUL LAA YABGHEYAAN.\nThere is a barrier between them, which they do not overstep.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(21)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nيَخْرُجُ مِنْهُمَا اللُّؤْلُؤُ وَالْمَرْجَانُۚ‏(22)\nYAKHROJO MINHOMAL LO-LO-O WAL MARJAAN.\nFrom them emerge the pearl and the coral.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(23)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nوَلَهُ الْجَوَارِ الْمُنْشَئٰتُ فِى الْبَحْرِ كَالْاَعْلَامِۚ‏(24)\nWA LAHUL JAWAARIL MUNSHA-AATO FIL BAHRE KAL-A-A’LAAM.\nHis are the sailing ships on the sea [appearing] like landmarks.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(25)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nكُلُّ مَنْ عَلَيْهَا فَانٍ ۚ ۖ‏(26)\nKULLO MAN A’LAYHAA FAANIN.\nEveryone on it is ephemeral,\nوَّيَبْقٰى وَجْهُ رَبِّكَ ذُو الْجَلٰلِ وَالْاِكْرَامِۚ‏(27)\nWA YABQAA WAJHO RABBEKA ZUL-JALAALE WAL-IKRAAM.\nyet lasting is the majestic and munificent Face of your Lord.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(28)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nيَسْئَلُهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ كُلَّ يَوْمٍ هُوَ فِىْ شَاْنٍۚ‏(29)\nYAS-ALOHU MAN FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZ, KULLA YAWMIN HOWA FEE SHAAN.\nEveryone in the heavens and the earth asks Him. Every day He is engaged in some work.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(30)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nسَنَفْرُغُ لَكُمْ اَيُّهَ الثَّقَلٰنِۚ‏(31)\nSANAFROGHO LAKUM AYYOHAS SAQALAAN.\nSoon We shall make Ourselves unoccupied for you, O you notable two!\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(32)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nيٰمَعْشَرَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ اِنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ اَنْ تَنْفُذُوْا مِنْ اَقْطَارِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ فَانْفُذُوْاؕ لَا تَنْفُذُوْنَ اِلَّا بِسُلْطٰنٍۚ‏(33)\nYAA MA’SHARAL JINNE WAL INSE ENIS TA-TA’TUM AN TANFOZOO MIN AQTAARIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE FANFOZOO, LAA TANFOZOONA ILLAA BE SULTAAN.\nO company of jinn and humans! If you can pass through the confines of the heavens and the earth, then do pass through. But you will not pass through except by an authority [from Allah].\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(34)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nيُرْسَلُ عَلَيْكُمَا شُوَاظٌ مِّنْ نَّارٍ ۙ وَّنُحَاسٌ فَلَا تَنْتَصِرٰنِۚ‏(35)\nYURSALO A’LAYKOMAA SHOWAAZUM MIN NAARINW, WA NOHAASUN FALAA TANTASERAAN.\nThere will be unleashed upon you a flash of fire and a smoke; then you will not be able to help one another.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(36)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفَاِذَا انْشَقَّتِ السَّمَآءُ فَكَانَتْ وَرْدَةً كَالدِّهَانِۚ‏(37)\nFA-EZAN SHAQQATIS SAMAAA-O FA-KAANAT WARDATAN KAD-DEHAAN.\nWhen the sky is split open, and turns crimson like tanned leather.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(38)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفَيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا يُسْئَلُ عَنْ ذَنْۢبِهٖۤ اِنْسٌ وَّلَا جَآنٌّۚ‏(39)\nFA YAWMA-EZIL LAA YUS-ALO A’N ZANBEHI INSUNW WA LAA JAAAN.\nOn that day neither humans will be questioned about their sins nor jinn.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(40)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nيُعْرَفُ الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ بِسِيْمٰهُمْ فَيُؤْخَذُ بِالنَّوَاصِىْ وَ الْاَقْدَامِۚ‏(41)\nYO’RAFUL MUJREMOONA BE SEEMAAHUM FA-YOO-KHAZO BIN NAWAASEE WAL AQDAAM.\nThe guilty will be recognized by their mark; so they will be seized by their forelocks and feet.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(42)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nهٰذِهٖ جَهَنَّمُ الَّتِىْ يُكَذِّبُ بِهَا الْمُجْرِمُوْنَۘ‏(43)\nHAAZEHI JAHANNAMUL LATEE YOKAZZEBO BEHAL MUJREMOON.\n‘This is the hell which the guilty would deny!’\nيَطُوْفُوْنَ بَيْنَهَا وَبَيْنَ حَمِيْمٍ اٰنٍۚ‏(44)\nYATOOFOONA BAYNAHAA WA BAYNA HAMEEMIN AAN.\nThey shall circuit between it and boiling hot water.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(45)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nوَلِمَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ جَنَّتٰنِۚ‏(46)\nWA LEMAN KHAAFA MAQAAMA RABBEHI JANNATAAN.\nFor him who stands in awe of his Lord will be two gardens.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۙ‏(47)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nذَوَاتَاۤ اَفْنَانٍۚ‏(48)\nZAWAATAA AFNAAN.\nBoth abounding in branches.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(49)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفِيْهِمَا عَيْنٰنِ تَجْرِيٰنِۚ‏(50)\nFEEHEMAA A’YNAANE TAJREYAAN.\nIn both of them will be two flowing springs.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(51)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAANE.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفِيْهِمَا مِنْ كُلِّ فَاكِهَةٍ زَوْجٰنِۚ‏(52)\nFEEHEMAA MIN KULLE FAAKEHATIN ZAWJAAN.\nIn both of them will be two kinds of every fruit.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(53)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى فُرُشٍۢ بَطَآئِنُهَا مِنْ اِسْتَبْرَقٍؕ وَجَنَی الْجَنَّتَيْنِ دَانٍۚ‏(54)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAA FOROSHIM BATAAA-ENOHAA MIN ISTABRAQIN, WA JANAL JANNATAYNE DAAN.\n[They will be] reclining on beds lined with green silk. And the fruit of the two gardens will be near at hand.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(55)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفِيْهِنَّ قٰصِرٰتُ الطَّرْفِۙ لَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ اِنْسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَآنٌّۚ‏(56)\nFEEHINNA QAASERAATUT TARFE, LAM YATMISHUNNA INSUN QABLAHUM WALAA JAAAN.\nIn them are maidens of restrained glances, whom no human has touched before, nor jinn.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ ۚ‏(57)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nكَاَنَّهُنَّ الْيَاقُوْتُ وَالْمَرْجَانُۚ‏(58)\nKA-ANNAHUNNAL YAAQOOTO WAL MARJAAN.\nAs though they were rubies and corals.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(59)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nهَلْ جَزَآءُ الْاِحْسَانِ اِلَّا الْاِحْسَانُۚ‏(60)\nHAL JAZAAA-UL EHSAANE ILLAL EHSAAN.\nIs the requital of goodness anything but goodness?\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(61)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nوَمِنْ دُوْنِهِمَا جَنَّتٰنِۚ‏(62)\nWA MIN DOONEHEMAA JANNATAAN.\nBeside these two, there will be two [other] gardens.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۙ‏(63)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nمُدْهَآمَّتٰنِۚ‏(64)\nMUD-HAAMMATAAN.\nDark green.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(65)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفِيْهِمَا عَيْنٰنِ نَضَّاخَتٰنِۚ‏(66)\nFEEHEMAA A’YNAANE NAZZAAKHATAAN.\nIn both of them will be two gushing springs.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(67)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفِيْهِمَا فَاكِهَةٌ وَّنَخْلٌ وَّرُمَّانٌۚ‏(68)\nFEEHEMAA FAAKEHATUNW WA NAKHLUNW WA RUMMAAN.\nIn both of them will be fruits, date-palms and pomegranates.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(69)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nفِيْهِنَّ خَيْرٰتٌ حِسَانٌۚ‏(70)\nFEEHINNA KHAYRAATUN HESAAN.\nIn them are maidens good and lovely.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(71)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nحُوْرٌ مَّقْصُوْرٰتٌ فِى الْخِيَامِۚ‏(72)\nHOORUM MAQSOORAATUN FIL KHEYAAM.\nHouris secluded in pavilions.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(73)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nلَمْ يَطْمِثْهُنَّ اِنْسٌ قَبْلَهُمْ وَلَا جَآنٌّۚ‏(74)\nLAM YAT-MISHUNNA INSUN QABLAHUM WA LAA JAAAN.\nWhom no human has touched before, nor jinn.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِۚ‏(75)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى رَفْرَفٍ خُضْرٍ وَّعَبْقَرِىٍّ حِسَانٍۚ‏(76)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAA RAFRAFIN KHUZRINW WA A’BQARIYYIN HESAAN.\nReclining on green cushions and lovely carpets.\nفَبِاَىِّ اٰلَاۤءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبٰنِ‏(77)\nFABE-AYYE AALAAA-E RABBEKOMAA TOKAZZEBAAN.\nSo which of your Lord’s bounties will you both deny?\nتَبٰرَكَ اسْمُ رَبِّكَ ذِى الْجَلٰلِ وَالْاِكْرَامِ‏(78)\nTABAARAKAS-MO RABBEKA ZIL JALAALE WAL IKRAAM.\nBlessed is the Name of your Lord, the Majestic and the Munificent!",
  "merits": "This Surah has 78 verses and it is ‘Makki’. Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that reciting this Surah on Friday after the dawn prayers carries great reward. Surah as-Rahman removes hypocrisy from one’s heart.\nOn the Day of Judgement, this Surah will come in the shape of a human being who will be handsome and will have a very nice scent. Allah (s.w.t.) will then tell him to point out those people who used to recite this Surah and he will name them. Then he will be allowed to beg pardon for those whom he names and Allah (s.w.t.) will pardon them.\nThe Imam (a.s.) also said that if a person dies after reciting this Surah, then is considered a martyr. Writing this Surah and keeping it makes all difficulties and problems vanish and also cures eye ailments. Writing it on the walls of a house keeps away all types of household pests. If recited at night, then Allah (s.w.t.) sends an angel to guard the reciter until he wakes up and if recited in the daytime then an angel guards him until sunset."
